Copyright notices and terms
===========================

Where the sources come from
---------------------------

The system in sys/ is the Lisp Machine system of the Massachusetts Institute
of Technology, System 99.32, as recovered from TID/671 by MIT's Tapes of Tech
Square project: a backup of the machine OZ.

LM-3 brought that content up as System 100 (https://tumbleweed.nu/r/sys).
That work, every commit of it, is Alfred M. Szmidt's, who commits there as ams.
The release note for System 100 declares:

    Everything is now licensed under the terms of the GNU Affero General
    Public License as published by the Free Software Foundation, either
    version 3 of the License, or (at your option) any later version.

This system is forked from System 100 and is distributed under the same terms. The
full licence text is in LICENSE.

Fixes from LM-3's later work
----------------------------

Some fixes were taken from the changes LM-3 made after System 100, on its way
to System 304: each one singly, checked against these files, and none bringing
material from LMI's or Gigamos's System 130. They are LM-3's work, all of them
committed by Alfred M. Szmidt (ams), covered by the same declaration and
distributed under the same terms.
docs/upstream-changes.md, in the repository, lists each one.

